                <div class="cntimage"><!-- ←20140212 -->
          <time datetime="2026-10-01T12:50:00+09:00" class="yeartime">Oct 01, 2026  12:50:00</time>
          <h1 class="title">Ollama supports the execution of Jev-like decision models.</h1>
          <!-- google_ad_section_start -->
         <p class="preface"></p><a href="https://i.gzn.jp/img/2026/10/01/ollama-jev-style-decision-models/00.png" target="_blank"><div style="aspect-ratio:16/9;max-width:560px;width:100%;display:inline-block;"><img src="https://i.gzn.jp/img/2026/10/01/ollama-jev-style-decision-models/00_m.png" border="0" alt="" class="lzsmall"></div></a><p class="preface"><br><br> The AI execution environment Ollama now supports the execution of decision-making models designed with the same ideas as <b><a href="https://gigazine.net/news/20260916-system-one-jev/" target="_blank">Jev</a></b> . As of the time of writing, three types are available for execution: ' <b><a href="https://ollama.com/library/nimble" target="_blank">Nimble</a></b> ', ' <b><a href="https://ollama.com/library/tev1" target="_blank">Tev1</a></b> ', and ' <b><a href="https://ollama.com/library/tev1:0.8b" target="_blank">Tev1:0.8b</a></b> '.<br><br> <b>Ollama now supports Jev-style decision models · Ollama Blog</b><br> <b><a href="https://ollama.com/blog/ollama-now-supports-jev-style-decision-models" target="_blank">https://ollama.com/blog/ollama-now-supports-jev-style-decision-models</a></b><br><br></p><blockquote class="twitter-tweet"><p lang="en" dir="ltr"> Ollama now supports Jev-like decision models all locally.<br><br> Use decision models like Nimble for tasks like ticket triaging, model routing, and content moderation.<br><br> Ollama pull nimble<br><br> Here&#39;s Nimble playing Ollama racer through the new local /v1/systemone API by making decisions in… <a href="https://t.co/HPLMmxcTSj">pic.twitter.com/HPLMmxcTSj</a></p> — ollama (@ollama) <a href="https://x.com/ollama/status/2105152056382345544?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">September 30, 2026</a></blockquote><p class="preface"><br></p><script async src="https://platform.x.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script><p class="preface"><br><br> Jev is an AI model developed with a fundamentally different approach from large-scale language models (LLMs), and can output 'judgments' and 'confidence scores' for choices. Because Jev can be executed quickly and at low cost when used appropriately, there is a growing movement to use it in combination with existing AI models and applications. For example, the AI gateway service OpenRouter offers 'Jev Router,' which uses Jev to 'determine the best AI model for a task,' achieving a selection system that is faster and more accurate than existing automatic selection systems.<br><br> <b><a href="https://gigazine.net/news/20260928-openrouter-jev-router/" target="_blank">'Jev Router' has been released, which automatically selects which AI to use based on task difficulty. It can instantly determine the appropriate AI model based on task difficulty and is more accurate than existing OpenRouter routers - GIGAZINE<br></p><img src="https://i.gzn.jp/img/2026/09/28/openrouter-jev-router/00_m.png" border="0" alt="" class="lzsmall"><p class="preface"></a></b><br><br> Furthermore, 'decision-making models' that operate using a similar mechanism to Jev are appearing one after another, and on September 30, 2026, 'd1' was released, achieving a score that surpassed Jev in benchmark tests.<br><br> <b><a href="https://gigazine.net/news/20260930-d1-decision-model-liquid-ai/" target="_blank">Decision-making model 'd1' surpasses Jev in benchmarks - GIGAZINE<br></p><img src="https://i.gzn.jp/img/2026/09/30/d1-decision-model-liquid-ai/00.jpg" border="0" alt="" class="lzsmall"><p class="preface"></a></b><br><br> Ollama has announced support for running decision models. As of the time of writing, three models are supported: 'nimble,' 'tev1,' and 'tev1:0.8b.' You can run each model by updating to version 0.35. Details of each model can be found at the following link.<br><br> <b>Nimble</b><br> <b><a href="https://ollama.com/library/nimble" target="_blank">https://ollama.com/library/nimble</a></b><br><br> <b>Tev1</b><br> <b><a href="https://ollama.com/library/tev1" target="_blank">https://ollama.com/library/tev1</a></b><br><br> <b>Tev1:0.8b</b><br> <b><a href="https://ollama.com/library/tev1:0.8b" target="_blank">https://ollama.com/library/tev1:0.8b</a></b><br><br> Ollama has shared a video demonstrating how to use Nimble to play a racing game, making decisions such as 'move left or right.'<br></p><blockquote class="twitter-tweet"><p lang="en" dir="ltr"> Ollama now supports Jev-like decision models all locally.<br><br> Use decision models like Nimble for tasks like ticket triaging, model routing, and content moderation.<br><br> Ollama pull nimble<br><br> Here&#39;s Nimble playing Ollama racer through the new local /v1/systemone API by making decisions in… <a href="https://t.co/HPLMmxcTSj">pic.twitter.com/HPLMmxcTSj</a></p> — ollama (@ollama) <a href="https://x.com/ollama/status/2105152056382345544?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">September 30, 2026</a></blockquote><p class="preface"><br></p><script async src="https://platform.x.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script><p class="preface"><br><br> Ollama 0.35 is positioned as the first in a series of releases supporting decision-making models, and future updates are planned to include 'MLX support for faster operation on Macs' and 'increasing the number of supported models.'<br><br />
</p>
        </div>
        
        
